link_detection.c, above `static int frl_verify_restore;`:
cinemaONE test knob (2026-09-27, plan J's J021): the destructive HDMI FRL
verification turns the link's streams off (dpms) and nothing turns them back
on when the sink did not change, since amdgpu_dm re-commits only for a new
sink. 1 = remember the streams that were on, and after the verification turn
them back on if the verified rate still carries the rate they ran at.
0 = upstream.

link_detection.c, above `bool same_sink = streams[0]->sink == link->local_sink;`:
FRL streams only (a TMDS stream stays off, as upstream), and
only toward the same sink: a changed sink gets amdgpu_dm's
forced commit instead.

link_dpms.c, above `void link_set_streams_dpms_on_for_link(struct dc_link *link,`:
cinemaONE test (dc_hpo_frl_verify_restore=1, 2026-09-27): turn back on the
streams a destructive link verification turned off -- the second half of
link_restart_all_streams_for_link() -- each only while it is still in the
current state on this link with dpms off.

link_hdmi_frl.c, above `static bool frl_said_rate_down;`:
The restart's two gates (cinemaONE, 2026-09-27, plan J's J021), neither
counted by the cap, each said once until the next link enable:
 - LTP 0xF on a lane asks for a lower FRL rate, which a restart at the same
   rate cannot give: not served;
 - with no stream on the link (a destructive verification turned it off),
   there is nothing to restart: left to hotplug and userspace.

